  "notes": "Web 381 — ROUTE-SHEET-FILE-UPLOAD-NOV8 (owner, Nov 8, 2026: 16:38 “there has to be an option to upload the file!”; 16:43 “It should be In the Dispatch”; 16:47 “If file has them both”; 16:48 “Why would a user upload 2 separate”): the route-sheet intake MOVED from the Preferences Pay card to a ‘🚌 Route sheets’ card in the driver’s own Dispatch face, directly under Today’s dispatch — and gained the file door. The Photograph doors stay per run (a photo is of one printed sheet); the FILE door is ONE door: the company sends one file, the driver uploads it once, and the app sorts the runs itself — a file carrying both runs fills BOTH routes (each run’s stops in order, by the file’s own AM/PM shift sections, or each stop’s own AM/PM marking), a file carrying one run fills that run only, and a file whose runs cannot be told apart says so plainly and saves nothing. Reads: an image file goes through the haul-card reader (TicketOCR) exactly as the photo does; a PDF with a text layer is read as text (PDF.js); a PDF with no text layer is rendered page by page into the same OCR. Every save lands through SplitShift.setRouteSheet with the photo path’s note behaviour; a failed read saves nothing and never touches a saved route. The sample (Nirojini’s CBE-0574 export) carries three runs — AM, NOON, PM — in one file; the app’s route model is AM/PM, so NOON is never saved. modules/dispatch.js + modules/preferences.js only; version stays 63.",
